( 05/08/84 EXPERT-2  VERIFY SUPPORT                            )                                                                : VERIFY       ( HYP^  ---  TF )                                   'VERIFY  @  EXECUTE ;                                                                                                           \ THIS IS A VECTORED IMPLEMENTATION OF VERIFY.  IT              \ ALLOWS FORWARD REFERENCING OF THE ACTUAL DEFINITION TO        \ THE PRIMITIVE <VERIFY> .                                      \                                                               \ VERIFY CALLED FOR STRINGS, REPORTS TRUTH.  TESTIF+ THEN       \ CHECKS LOGIC FLAG.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( 05/08/84 EXPERT-2  VERIFY SUPPORT                            )                                                                : TESTIF+      ( R#  ---  TF )                                     FINDIF                                                            BEGIN   DUP @ 0=                                                  IF  ( NO MORE IFS, ALL FOUND TRUE )  DROP TRUE TRUE             ELSE  STRING?                                                     IF   DUP VERIFY   ( IF^, IF^ --- IF^, TF )                        SWAP GETLOGIC    ( TF, IF^, LF )                                0=              ( TRUE IF + LOGIC  )                            ROT XOR NOT       ( IF^, TF )                                 ELSE  ( EQN ) RUNEQN     ( CFA^, TF )                           THEN RULECK                                                   THEN                                                          UNTIL   RULE#DROP  ;                                                                                                       ( 05/08/84 EXPERT-2  VERIFY SUPPORT                            )                                                                : XCALL     ( STACK POINTER  --- TF  )                             BEGIN  DUP @ DUP                                                  IF SUBHYP^   @ @ =                                                IF  DROP TRUE FALSE   ( FOUND )                                 ELSE  TRUE        ( NOT FOUND YET )                             THEN                                                          ELSE DROP DROP FALSE  FALSE       ( NOT FOUND ANYWHERE )        THEN                                                          WHILE  2+    ( BUMP STACK POINTER  )                            REPEAT    ;                                                     \ XCALL SUPPORTS RECALL BY CHECKING FOR LAST ENTRY ON           \ STACK POINTER EQUAL.                                          \                                                               \ EXITS TRUE IF FOUND, FALSE IF NOT FOUND.                   ( 05/08/84 EXPERT-2  VERIFY SUPPORT                            )                                                                : RECALL    ( FACT^ --- TF, TRUE IF FOUND )                        SUBHYP^ !                                                       KNOWNTRUE XCALL                                                   IF TRUE TRUE           ( FOUND TRUE )                           ELSE               ( NOT FOUND TRUE )                             KNOWNFALSE   XCALL                                                IF  FALSE TRUE   ( FOUND FALSE )                                ELSE   FALSE   ( NOT FOUND ANYWHERE )                          THEN                                                         THEN    ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  